      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T18:18:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This duplicates the `union reg_interrupt` defined by tps6699x_reg.h.  Can you use the real header instead?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "5e4799f95c64fb8e6484f3f283bf3e475062eb34",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e545963_6a95bc40",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_tps6699x_private.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T20:24:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately the `tps6699x_reg.h` contain register/length info in its structs for sending over I2C bus. \n```\nunion reg_interrupt {\n\tstruct {\n\t\t/** Used for */\n\t\tuint8_t _intern_reg : 8;\n\t\tuint8_t _intern_len : 8;\n:\n```\nAlso, how would we catch any issues with bit offsets if we include the same file? I\u0027m not a fan of copy/paste, but I\u0027ll do a quick comparison against the data sheet for correctness.",
      "parentUuid": "09e08b14_7fc937d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "5e4799f95c64fb8e6484f3f283bf3e475062eb34",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97bc1940_402678a6",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_tps6699x_private.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-30T21:25:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We want to remove the `_inter_reg` and `_intern_len` fields from the driver, but this effort is blocked until we have unit tests to give us confidence in the change.\n\nIf this prevents the emulator from using this struct, that\u0027s fine for now, but it makes sense to use a unique name.\n\nRegarding catching bit offset errors - I think this is somewhat of a corner case and not needed in the unit test.  A better check would be to just add a build_assert that overall size of the struct is correct.",
      "parentUuid": "9e545963_6a95bc40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "5e4799f95c64fb8e6484f3f283bf3e475062eb34",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
